{{ lookup('vars', card.prompt_var) }}

EVIDENCE CONTRACT (mandatory for any finding, number, count, index, host, or status you report): every such value MUST come from a tool result you actually received THIS run. Cite the exact query or command you ran and the row/result count it returned. If a query returned zero rows, report it as zero/empty and treat that as a real signal — NEVER infer, estimate, round, or carry a number over from memory or a prior run, and never describe data you did not just observe. If your tools were unavailable or every query failed, say so and call kanban_block (kind=needs_input) — do NOT invent a result. A completion summary that reports findings without the query and the counts behind them is INCOMPLETE and will be rejected by the goal judge; do not kanban_complete it.

When finished, deliver a FULL REPORT to Slack — not a one-line summary. That post is this card's primary output and, for most cards, the only thing the operator ever sees; a sentence where a report belongs is a silent downgrade. Use the terminal command `hermes send --to slack:{{ hermes_agent_slack_hermes_all_channel }} --quiet '<report>'`. The report leads with ONE headline line saying what the run concluded, then the concrete findings: the actual values, counts, statuses, names or ids you observed THIS run, one per line, each traceable to the query or command that produced it (the evidence contract above applies to every line of it). A check that came back clean is a finding — say what you checked and what it returned; do not drop it and do not summarize a set of checks as "all healthy" without naming them. Zero rows, an unreachable endpoint and a failed command are each reported as themselves. Keep it under 25 lines, plain text, no Markdown tables. Then call kanban_complete with a ONE-LINE summary (the headline) plus metadata: that summary field feeds the board digest, so it must stay a single line even though the Slack post is long. The native sender already owns the configured Slack credentials: do not inspect environment variables, search for webhooks, or call Slack with curl. If the native sender fails because delivery configuration or operator input is required, call kanban_block with kind=needs_input and the reason. NEVER end the run with text alone: only a successful kanban_complete or kanban_block tool call ends the card. Do NOT block for human review — decide and act within your tool policy.
